strTrim [SimTalk]
Returns a string from which Plant Simulation removed leading and trailing blanks, tab stops, and carriage
returns.
Type
Function
Syntax
strTrim(Text:string) → string
Parameter
The parameter Text of data type string designates the string, which contains leading and trailing blanks,
tab stops, and carriage returns, i.e., whitespace characters.
Return Value
The return value has the data type string.
Examples
print strTrim(" ab c ") // returns "ab c"
strTrim("  hello  ") = strTrim("hello    ") -- ignores leading and trailing 
spaces
