CalendarWeek [SimTalk]
Returns the calendar week of the specified date according to DIN 1355/ ISO 8601.
Remarks
A new week always starts on Monday.
According to DIN 1355/ ISO 8601 the first calendar week of a year is the first week that contains at least
four days of the new year.
Note
Plant Simulation uses the Date and Time Format of the Model Language you selected.
Type
Function
Syntax
CalendarWeek(Date:dateTime) → integer
Parameter
The parameter Date of data type dateTime designates the date.
Return Value
The return value has the data type integer.
CalendarWeek [SimTalk]
Plant Simulation Help 12-349
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Examples
print CalendarWeek(str_to_date("2023/11/21")) // returns 47, model language 
English
print CalendarWeek(str_to_date("21.11.2023")) // returns 47, model language 
German
See also
Date and Time Format [model settings]
Model Language [model settings]
